 ratings.", "Incumbent Kat Cammack (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Kat Cammack seeks another term in this heavily Republican North Florida district, where the partisan lean favors her party by about ten points. She enters the fall with a decisive financial advantage, more than $2 million raised and nearly $880,000 on hand, while Democratic nominee Seth Harp has raised under $40,000 and has little cash to compete. An independent candidate trails far behind in both money and visibility.\n\nEvery major expert rating, from Cook and Inside Elections to Sabato and Split Ticket, places the race in the Solid or Safe Republican column, and prediction markets give Cammack roughly a 94% chance of winning. Her recent headlines emphasize federal funding for veterans housing, water infrastructure, and rural health, reinforcing an incumbent-friendly picture. No public polling is available, but the combination of district lean, incumbency, and money leaves little doubt about the expected outcome.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0356, "margin": -14.68}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0357, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0316, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0435, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0175, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0207, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0246, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0139, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0233, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0338, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.018, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.018, "margin": -14.0}]}